think The inner prompt's latest revisions are a run of about a hundred held laps, each waiting on a ruling for P1. I searched for where P1 is defined. It is not in the card or the seat prompt. It is a precondition in the sawtooth sweep paper, active-designing/date/20261011/20261011-123141_the-sawtooth-sweep-26-to-31-no-discriminating-count.md.
think P1 requires every miss ratio below 1.05 on both arms. P2 requires a nonzero conflict count in each pair on both arms. That paper reports that the Cartesian arm shows zero conflict misses at every count and every N, so P2 cannot pass under the literal both-arms reading at any set count from 26 to 31.
think A pre-registered falsifier that cannot pass by construction is a finding about the falsifier. Restating or retiring it after seeing the table would be a post-hoc edit, and the logs reserve that ruling for Keaton or Claude. So this lap records the diagnosis and does not restate P1.
obs Observation, read from the sawtooth paper: F4 fired as written, and the paper says P2 fails at every count on the Cartesian arm. No new measurement was made this lap.
obs Inference: the hold is caused by an unsatisfiable precondition, not by a lack of work. Each repeated hold log restated that P1 was unruled without naming why it cannot be ruled into a pass.
obs Projection, horizon one sitting: the stall clears only when someone restates P2 as a per-arm or Polar-only condition, or retires the sawtooth falsifier as failed. Falsifier: if a P2 reading exists under which the Cartesian arm can pass, this diagnosis is wrong and the hold is a plain ruling wait.
